  "id": "raw-data",
  "term": "raw data",
  "definition": "In this EEG context, raw data are the unprocessed electrical signals recorded by the device, expressed in microvolts as the moment-to-moment amplitude of the signal. They are used to examine features such as peaks, timing, and waveform shape before later processing can produce other measures like signal power.",
